note F38: CPython Lib/concurrent/futures/_base.py, Future.set_result
note "Should only be used by Executor implementations and unit tests." is a usage rule in the docstring; the doc has no visibility or "friend" construct, so it is kept as this note only

choice FutureState
    Pending
    Running
    Cancelled
    Cancelled_and_notified
    Finished

type Future
    field state as a FutureState
    note GAP: dynamic typing of the result - the original stores any Python object; the doc has no "any" type, so Value stands for an unconstrained type parameter that the doc cannot declare on Future
    field result as a maybe Value
    note GAP: shared mutable state guarded by a condition variable - a Future is written by a worker thread and read by waiting threads; the doc forbids values shared mutably between tasks (example 38) and has no lock or condition type, so Condition is invented
    field condition as a Condition
    note GAP: interfaces and dynamic dispatch - waiters are objects of several classes (_FirstCompletedWaiter, _AllCompletedWaiter, ...) that each implement add_result differently; Waiter is used as if it were an interface
    field waiters as a List of Waiter
    note GAP: stored callbacks - done callbacks are functions added by users and called later; there is no type for an operation held as a value
    field done_callbacks as a List of Operation taking a Future

to add_result of future to waiter
    note GAP: an operation with one body per kind of waiter, chosen at run time; the doc has no interface or method declaration, so this header stands for that dispatch
    given future is a Future
    given waiter is an editable Waiter

to invoke_callbacks of future
    given future is a Future
    uses callbacks of future

to set_result result on future
    given result is a Value
    note GAP: shared reference - future must be visible to other threads while this operation changes it; `editable` gives exclusive ownership, which is the opposite of what a Future is for
    given future is an editable Future
    fails with InvalidStateError
    note UNCLEAR: the waiters and callbacks may do anything; the doc gives no way to say "uses whatever the waiters and callbacks use"
    uses condition of future, callbacks of future

    note GAP: locks - `with self._condition:` acquires the condition's lock for the block and releases it on every exit; `hold` (example 19) releases a resource on every exit, so it is borrowed here, but the doc defines `hold` only for opening resources, not for acquiring a lock
    hold guard as acquire condition of future
        if state of future is Cancelled or state of future is Cancelled_and_notified or state of future is Finished
            note WORKAROUND: the failure carries the message '{state}: {future!r}' in Python; the doc's `fail with` shows only bare failure names, so the message text cannot be attached; the repr of the future also has no Scribe equivalent
            fail with InvalidStateError
        set result of future to some result
        set state of future to Finished
        note GAP: shared mutable references - iterating the waiters and changing each one through the list; `for each` binds read-only items in every doc example, so whether a loop variable can be changed is not covered
        for each waiter in waiters of future
            add_result of future to waiter
        note GAP: condition variables - notify_all wakes every thread waiting on the condition; the doc's structured concurrency has no way to wait for, or signal, another task
        notify_all condition of future
    invoke_callbacks of future
